 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Victoria's unemployment rate is higher. In September 2026 (seasonally adjusted, the latest data available), Victoria was **5.1%** and NSW was **4.7%**, a gap of about **0.35 percentage points**.\n\nThe gap has been widening. In January 2026 NSW was slightly higher (4.2% vs 4.1%... Victoria was 4.2% and NSW 4.2%), so the two were roughly level. Victoria has been above NSW every month since February, and NSW rose faster over the year, from 4.2% to 4.7%, while Victoria went from 4.2% to 5.1%. Monthly state figures are noisy, so the September gap could move in later releases.",
